1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,404
Every tonne of Turkish steel entering the EU now carries a carbon bill.

2
00:00:06,624 --> 00:00:13,081
Since 1 January 2026, importers pay for the emissions embedded in what they bring in.

3
00:00:13,301 --> 00:00:16,585
But nobody can see the CO₂ in a steel coil.

4
00:00:16,805 --> 00:00:22,088
So an importer can trust a number it cannot check, or pay a default value plus a mark-up.

5
00:00:22,308 --> 00:00:27,181
10% in 2026. 20% in 2027. 30% from 2028.

6
00:00:27,401 --> 00:00:30,054
That punishes exactly the mills that cleaned up.

7
00:00:30,884 --> 00:00:35,421
EmbedProof makes the claim checkable, and the tonne impossible to sell twice.

8
00:00:35,641 --> 00:00:39,727
First, an AI model asks whether the number is plausible for this plant.

9
00:00:39,947 --> 00:00:48,090
Then it is signed twice: one classical signature, one post-quantum signature, because these records are kept for years.

10
00:00:48,310 --> 00:00:53,435
A smart contract anchors the result, and refuses to hand the same tonne to two buyers.

11
00:00:53,655 --> 00:00:57,164
Anything the model flags goes to a human verifier first.

12
00:00:57,994 --> 00:01:07,594
Marmara Demir, a fictional scrap-fed mill, reports 0.535 tCO₂ per tonne of steel for September.

13
00:01:07,814 --> 00:01:13,724
The model checks it against what this route, size and grid can emit, and the plant's own history.

14
00:01:13,944 --> 00:01:17,595
Inside the expected range: risk 20, green.

15
00:01:18,065 --> 00:01:25,924
The mill signs. The attestor adds two signatures and anchors the batch on chain: about 228,000 gas.

16
00:01:26,754 --> 00:01:35,467
Anadolu Entegre, a fictional blast-furnace mill, reports 0.56: a figure only an electric-arc mill could reach.

17
00:01:35,687 --> 00:01:42,506
The model expected about 2.3. Its reasons are listed: the production route, and the plant's own history.

18
00:01:42,726 --> 00:01:48,615
Risk 100. Red. The batch is held for a verifier, and its tonnes cannot be allocated.

19
00:01:49,035 --> 00:01:55,951
The verifier unseals the report, reads those reasons, and overrides it, with a written reason pinned to the batch.

20
00:01:56,781 --> 00:02:03,307
Back to the honest batch: 5,000 verified tonnes, all allocated to Importer A.

21
00:02:03,527 --> 00:02:06,597
Now the same 5,000 tonnes, to Importer B.

22
00:02:07,667 --> 00:02:13,101
The contract reverts. Double claim blocked: 5,000 requested, 0 remaining.

23
00:02:13,321 --> 00:02:18,919
Double claiming is treated like double spending: the cap is enforced on chain.

24
00:02:19,749 --> 00:02:26,436
Importer A scans the certificate's QR code. No wallet, no login: every check runs in the browser.

25
00:02:26,656 --> 00:02:30,002
Both signatures verify, including the post-quantum one.

26
00:02:30,222 --> 00:02:35,177
Now change one digit: 0.535 becomes 0.534.

27
00:02:35,897 --> 00:02:40,230
The fingerprint no longer matches the chain, and neither signature validates.

28
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:51,383
Why now: CBAM's definitive phase has begun, Türkiye's emissions trading pilot covers the same sectors, and the EU is its largest trading partner.

29
00:02:51,603 --> 00:02:57,405
Without verified data, a cleaner mill pays the same default plus mark-up as everyone else.

30
00:02:57,625 --> 00:03:07,122
For one shipment: tonnes × (default + mark-up − verified actual) × EU carbon price. Illustrative, demo data.

31
00:03:07,342 --> 00:03:12,228
EmbedProof makes the real figure cheap to trust, and impossible to count twice.

32
00:03:12,448 --> 00:03:19,646
And with COP31 opening in Antalya on 9 November, this is implementation, not another pledge.

33
00:03:20,476 --> 00:03:28,020
Not accredited CBAM verification. No offsets. No Article 6.

34
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:32,774
The chain guarantees integrity after data entry, not the truth of the data.

35
00:03:32,994 --> 00:03:37,332
The model measures consistency with Climate TRACE, not real emissions.

36
00:03:37,552 --> 00:03:46,950
With plant history it catches 97% of half-size under-reports. With no history, 84%: that misses our 90% target.

37
00:03:47,170 --> 00:03:56,701
178 contract tests, 100% coverage. Next: a 2-of-3 attestor quorum, zero-knowledge range proofs, a permissioned Besu network.

38
00:03:56,921 --> 00:04:00,053
EmbedProof. Check the claim. Block the double sale.

